# Internationalization

## Routing

Configured in `astro.config.mjs`:

- Locales: `fr` (default), `en`
- `prefixDefaultLocale: true` → all URLs are `/{locale}/...`

Mirror page structure across locales:

```
src/pages/fr/index.astro  ↔  src/pages/en/index.astro
src/pages/fr/recipes/[slug].astro  ↔  src/pages/en/recipes/[slug].astro
```

## Locale helpers (`src/lib/recipes.ts`)

- `getLocaleFromId(id)` — extract locale from content id (`fr/ratatouille`)
- `getSlugFromId(id)` — extract slug without locale prefix
- `getRecipesByLocale(locale)` — filtered, date-sorted collection
- `getAlternateRecipe(recipe, targetLocale)` — find translation via `translationKey`

## Language switcher

`LanguageSwitcher.astro` links to the alternate locale's recipe using `translationKey` matching. When adding a recipe, always provide both locale files or the switcher won't appear.

## UI copy

Hardcode locale-specific labels in page templates (e.g. difficulty labels, section headings). Keep fr/en page files in sync structurally — only copy and `locale` constant differ.
